# Apps whose Allow Notifications must be Off
# (System Settings → Notifications → the app → Allow notifications).
# macconfig-check.sh reads the usernoted group plist via lib/notification-prefs.py
# and warns (Needs Paul) when one of these has Allow Notifications on. It never
# writes the store, and there is no --fix for this.
#
# This is the whole list. Anything else may stay on. Do not add Cursor, Cursor
# Nightly, Find My, Finder, Ghostty, Google Chrome, Grok Bot, Hammerspoon,
# Microsoft Teams, Slack, Spotify, Tailscale, the Safari web app, Zoom, or company
# tools (Santa, SentinelAgent, Kerberos). On is not drift for those.
#
# Messages shows "Critical" in System Settings when Allow notifications is off
# and Critical Alerts are still allowed. That is off, not drift. The check
# reads flags bit 25 only. It does not require Critical Alerts off.
#
# One bundle id per line. Text after # is the display name (keep it in the
# notifications-apps title in lib/manual-steps.list). Blank lines and lines
# beginning with # are ignored.

com.apple.iCal # Calendar
com.apple.FaceTime # FaceTime
com.apple.gamecenter # Game Center
com.apple.Home # Home
com.apple.tips # Tips
com.apple.Passbook # Wallet
com.apple.MobileSMS # Messages
